{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And the man, wondering at her, kept silent.</b> Meaning: because he saw that his way had succeeded, and beyond what he had said in his condition the righteous woman herself said, his soul was pressing to say to her what he said shortly after — for the condition he had stipulated, ״וְאָמְרָה וְגַם לִגְמַלֶּיךָ אֶשְׁאָב״ (Genesis 24:44), was already fulfilled. Behold, she said ״וְגַם״ etc., and she fulfilled her words, as it is written (Genesis 24:20) ״וַתִּשְׁאַב לְכָל גְּמַלָּיו״, and he should not have needed to wait until the camels finished drinking, since this was not part of the condition. But he kept himself silent from speaking until he knew what she said — to water his camels until they finished drinking — and even though this matter is not part of the condition, because of her words a doubt arose in him concerning her: perhaps she is one of those who say much and do little. Once he saw that the camels had finished etc., he immediately gave the bracelets etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:07.445924479Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}